## What BLINK Is — And What It Remains

To be absolutely clear: this implementation plan does NOT change BLINK's identity or core algorithm. Here is what BLINK is and continues to be:

| Aspect | Before (Synthetic POC) | After (This Plan) |
|---|---|---|
| **Core algorithm** | Bidirectional RAFT flow + backward warping + flow-consistency blending | **Same** — no architectural changes |
| **Data source** | `SyntheticMOSDACSimulator` (numpy math) | **Real INSAT-3DS HDF5 from MOSDAC** + GOES for dev/training |
| **Cloudburst detection** | Magic numbers (arbitrary thresholds) | **NETRA-calibrated sigmoid model** with published thresholds |
| **Cyclone intensity** | `flow_mag * 4.2 + 65` (meaningless) | **Dvorak ADT CI estimation** with Courtney-Knaff P-W |
| **Validation** | Against own synthetic ground truth | **Against GOES 1-min mesoscale ground truth** |
| **User interaction** | Fixed scenario dropdown | **Date/time/region/source selector** fetching real data |
| **What BLINK is NOT** | ❌ NWP model, ❌ super-resolution, ❌ satellite command | **Same** — no scope creep |

